<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Radon fan replacement is the most common repair on an existing radon system, because the fan is the only part that moves. The pipe, the sealed slab and the sealed sump just sit there. The fan runs day and night, every day of the year, and Health Canada says it should never be turned off. Sooner or later it wears out.</p><p>This page is for Winnipeg, Regina and Saskatoon homeowners (and everyone in the towns around them) who already have a system, or who have a capped radon pipe in the basement floor that nobody ever connected. We put you in touch with an independent radon professional who checks the whole system, not just the fan, and quotes the job. If you have no system and no test yet, start with <a href="/radon-testing/">a long-term radon test</a> instead.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Fan swap on an existing system</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The failed fan comes out and a replacement sized for your pipe and suction points goes in. The rest of the system stays put.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Manometer check</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The U-tube manometer on the pipe is read and checked. If both sides of the liquid sit level, the system isn't pulling and the professional works out why.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Noise and vibration diagnosis</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A rattle or hum can be a worn fan, a loose mount or pipe touching the framing. Only one of those needs a new fan.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Cold-weather check</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Health Canada warns that fans in garages and attics can collect condensation and ice in the cold months, which can damage the fan. That matters here.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Rough-in activation</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Newer homes often have a capped radon pipe under the basement floor. A fan and exhaust piping turn it into a working system, if a test says you need one.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6E0D2;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#16263B;margin:0 0 8px;">Retest plan</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">After a fan swap or a basement renovation you get clear advice on which test to run, where to put it and for how long.</p>
      </div>
</div>
